// Task 5071 (κ) — engine-build hardening PRD §8 leaf κ, INV-GEO-2 (#4351)
// engine-build CONSUMER-side boundary test.
//
// Fixture for
// mixed_kernel_attribute_selectors_builds_renders_and_reads_per_kernel_attributes
// and mixed_kernel_attribute_selector_resolves_frame_on_build_path in
// crates/reify-eval/tests/manifold_cross_kernel_real.rs.
//
// A mixed-kernel module: an OCCT-resident cylinder ("post", realization
// index 0) coexists with a cross-kernel Mesh-demanded box union ("body",
// the terminal — highest-index — realization). No #kernel(...) pragma —
// Manifold routing is demanded-repr-driven: build(ExportFormat::Stl) causes
// compute_demanded_reprs to mark the terminal realization Mesh, which makes
// the dispatcher route the union to Manifold (Mesh-capable), preceded by an
// OCCT BRep→Mesh tessellation stage for its box operands, while "post"
// stays a plain OCCT BRep solid.
//
// Terminal-realization invariant (load-bearing): "body" MUST be declared
// LAST (so it has the highest realization index) and "post" declared
// BEFORE it. topology_attribute_table is reset once at the start of each
// top-level build()/tessellate_*() call, so this ordering keeps the union
// as this module's terminal realization; its op cone [box_a, box_b, union]
// seeds box_a/box_b on OCCT ({Occt,·} face entries) and those attributes
// are forwarded onto {Manifold,·} ingest handles during the
// convert-to-Manifold step, so a post-build topology_attribute_table holds
// BOTH kernels' entries side by side without one overwriting the other
// under the same numeric id — the class of collision task #4351 eliminates
// by re-keying the table on the full KernelHandle rather than a bare
// GeometryHandleId.
//
// Box geometry (mirrors examples/multi_kernel/manifold_boolean.ri):
//   box_a = box(10mm, 10mm, 10mm) — first box at origin.
//   box_b_raw = box(10mm, 10mm, 10mm) — second box before translation.
//   box_b = translate(box_b_raw, offset, 0mm, 0mm) — shifted `offset` (5mm)
//   in X (50% overlap with box_a along X, common slab x∈[0,5]mm).
//   body = union(box_a, box_b) — the terminal Mesh-demanded realization.
//
// Named bindings are required so compute_demanded_reprs can resolve the
// sub-refs (GeomRef::Sub) in the union op via name_to_idx — see
// manifold_boolean.ri's header for the full rationale.
//
// Syntax sources:
//   examples/multi_kernel/manifold_boolean.ri  (cross-kernel union core)
//   examples/ad_hoc_face_selector.ri           (@face attribute selector)
//   tests/prd-gate/fixtures/engine_build_hardening_kappa_mixed_kernel_selector.ri
//     (the PRD-gate probe that compile-pinned this exact combination,
//      2026-07-06, scripts/prd-capability-check.py exit 0)
//
// Entity name: MixedKernelAttributeSelectors
// Terminal realization let: body (highest realization index)

structure MixedKernelAttributeSelectors {
    // A named param is required so the eval-state value-cell graph has an
    // entry for entity "MixedKernelAttributeSelectors". Without at least
    // one param, propagate_subject_to_descendants returns [] →
    // active_tolerance_scope stays empty → demanded_tol = None →
    // RealizationCache insert is skipped → test_terminal_handle returns
    // None (mirrors manifold_boolean.ri's OverlapUnion param rationale).
    param offset : Length = 5mm

    // OCCT-resident primitive — realization index 0, declared FIRST so it
    // is never the terminal (highest-index) realization.
    let post = cylinder(4mm, 12mm)

    let box_a = box(10mm, 10mm, 10mm)
    let box_b_raw = box(10mm, 10mm, 10mm)
    let box_b = translate(box_b_raw, offset, 0mm, 0mm)
    let body = union(box_a, box_b)
}
